      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $x\\in (0,2),$ then $|x|<2.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in (0,2).$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $|x|<2.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin (0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin (0,2),$ or $|x|<2.$",
